# Moved: the canonical template is .env.local.example.
#
# Next.js loads .env.local for local development, so the template is named to match what you
# actually create (`cp .env.local.example .env.local`). This file is kept only so that older
# docs and bookmarks pointing at `.env.example` lead somewhere rather than nowhere.
#
# NOTE: the API variable was renamed and its FORMAT changed:
#   old: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/api/v1   (origin + version path)
#   new: NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080               (origin only)
# The /api/v1 prefix is now appended in lib/config/env.ts.
